  </table><div>


</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Note: On October 26, 2024,
the Ucommune Venture VIE Agreements were terminated and by which time Ucommune Venture and its subsidiaries were deconsolidated, and
certain businesses of the Company were disposed accordingly. The disposal of interior design and construction business represented a
strategic shift that had a major effect on the Company&#8217;s operations and financial results, and was accounted for as discontinued
operation. On July 21, 2025, we disposed a subsidiary which is the only subsidiary operates in marketing and branding service, upon which
we completely exited from all marketing and branding services operations. The disposal represented a strategic shift that had a major
effect on our operations and financial results, and was accounted for as discontinued operation. Our consolidated statements of operations
in this annual report separates the discontinued operations from our remaining business operations for all years presented. Please see
Note 4.b of the financial statements in this annual report.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"></p><div>

</div><!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 119; Value: 1 --><div>
    </div><div style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->112<!-- Field: /Sequence --></p></div><div>
    </div><div style="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><p style="margin: 0pt">&#160;</p></div><div>
    </div><!-- Field: /Page --><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b>Year Ended December 31, 2025 Compared to Year
Ended December 31, 2024</b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Net Revenue</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Our total net revenue from
continuing operations decreased by 66.2% to RMB26.1 million (US$3.7 million) in 2025 from RMB77.2 million in 2024. Revenues from our
asset-light model decreased by 57.3% to RMB15.0 million (US$2.1 million) in 2025 from RMB35.1 million in 2024.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><i>Workspace Membership Services Revenues</i></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Our workspace membership services
revenues decreased by 67.1% to RMB22.6 million (US$3.2 million) in 2025 from RMB68.6 million in 2024, primarily due to (1) the disposal
or closure of 21 self-operated spaces in FY2024, which contributed revenue of RMB24.5 million (US$3.5 million) with no such revenue in
FY2025; (2) the closure of 2 unprofitable self-operated spaces which were disposed of in 2025 and as a result, the revenue decreased RMB3.9
million (US$0.6 million) as compared to 2024; and (3) a decrease in revenue generated from U Partner category under our asset-light model
of RMB16.6 million (US$2.4 million) as a result of decreased number of spaces and expiration of large customer contract.</p><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><i>Other Services Revenues</i></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Our other services revenues
decreased by 59.8% to RMB3.5million (US$0.5 million) in 2025 from RMB8.7 million in 2024, primarily due to decreased revenue from U Brand
under our asset-light model of RMB3.1 million (US$0.4 million) as the number of spaces of this category decreased from 2 as of December
31, 2024 to nil as of December 31, 2025.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Cost of Revenue (Excluding Impairment Loss)</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Our total cost of revenue
(excluding impairment loss) from continuing operations decreased by 65.9% to RMB26.9 million (US$3.8 million) in 2025 from RMB79.0 million
in 2024. Cost of revenue from our asset-light model decreased by 63.2% to RMB12.3 million (US$1.8 million) in 2025 from RMB33.4 million
in 2024, which was in line with the decrease in revenues from our asset-light model businesses.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><i>Workspace Membership</i></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Our costs of workspace membership
decreased by 69.5% to RMB22.6 million (US$3.2 million) in 2025 from RMB74.1 million in 2024, primarily due to a decrease in operating
costs related to leases and staff along with the closure of unprofitable self-operated spaces in 2025. Our cost of revenue (excluding
impairment loss) for workspace membership accounted for 95.9% and 86.5% of our total net revenue in 2024 and 2025, respectively.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><i>Other Services</i></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Our costs of other services
decreased by 12.2% to RMB4.3 million (US$0.6 million) in 2025 from RMB4.9 million in 2024, which was generally in line with the decrease
in revenues. Our cost of revenue (excluding impairment loss) for other services accounted for 6.4% and 16.4% of our total net revenue
in 2024 and 2025, respectively.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Impairment Loss on Long-lived Assets and
Long-term Prepaid Expenses</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">We had impairment loss on
long-lived assets and long-term prepaid expenses of RMB2.9 million (US$0.4 million) in 2025, as compared to RMB1.0 million in 2024, primarily
due to impairment losses on right-of-use assets of RMB2.8 million (US$0.4 million) in 2025.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></p><div>

</div><!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 120; Value: 1 --><div>
    </div><div style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->113<!-- Field: /Sequence --></p></div><div>
    </div><div style="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><p style="margin: 0pt">&#160;</p></div><div>
    </div><!-- Field: /Page --><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Sales and Marketing Expenses</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Our sales and marketing expenses
decreased by 80.0% to RMB0.7 million (US$0.1 million) in 2025 from RMB3.5 million in 2024, mainly due to (1) a decrease in promotion
cost of RMB1.5 million (US$0.2 million) as a result of closure of spaces, and (2) a decrease in entertainment cost of RMB1.1 million
(US$0.2 million). Our sales and marketing expenses accounted for 4.6% and 2.7% of our total net revenue in 2024 and 2025, respectively.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>General and Administrative Expenses</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Our general and administrative
expenses decreased by 18.4% to RMB36.7 million (US$5.2 million) in 2025 from RMB45.0 million in 2024, mainly due to (1) a decrease in
staff cost of RMB6.4 million (US$0.9 million) due to we laid off certain employees in administrative and back-office departments, and
(2) a decrease in share-based compensation expenses of RMB1.4 million (US$0.2 million). Our general and administrative expenses accounted
for 58.2% and 140.4% of our total net revenue in 2024 and 2025, respectively. The increase in general and administrative expenses as
a percentage of total net revenue is mainly due to decreased revenue scale.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Change in Fair Value of Warrant Liability</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">We had a gain in change in
fair value of warrant liability of RMB0.5 million (US$0.1 million) in 2025 as compared to RMB4.9 million in 2024, primarily attributable
to the fair value decrease of warrants issued in a private placement on January 26, 2022.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>&#160;</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Loss from Operations</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">As a result of the foregoing,
our loss from operations was RMB40.6 million (US$5.8 million) in 2025, as compared to RMB46.3 million in 2024.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Interest (Expense)/Income, Net</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Our interest income, net
was RMB0.2 million (US$26 thousand) in 2025, as compared to interest expense, net of RMB2.3 million in 2024, due to the interest expense
accrued for third-party loans in 2024 while no such expenses in 2025 since the borrower Ucommune Venture was disposed of in 2024.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Subsidy Income</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Our subsidy income was subsidies
granted by local governments to support the development and operation of agile office spaces. Our subsidy income was RMB5 thousand (US1
thousand) in 2025, as compared to RMB0.8 million in 2024.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Impairment Loss on Long-term Investments</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Impairment loss on long-term
investments was nil in 2025, as compared to RMB18.0 million in 2024, primarily because the investee&#8217;s performance was stable in
2025 with no impairment recognized as compared with 2024.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Gain/(Loss) on Disposal of Subsidiaries</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">We had gain on disposal of
subsidiaries of RMB3.2 million (US$0.5 million) in 2025, as compared to loss on disposal of subsidiaries of RMB0.6 million in 2024, primarily
attributable to the disposal of subsidiaries with nil consideration that was at net liability position in 2025 compared with subsidiaries
at net asset position in 2024.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Other Income, Net</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">We had other income, net
of RMB0.7 million (US$0.1 million) in 2025, as compared with other income RMB2.2 million in 2024, mainly due to gain from asset transfer
in 2024 while no such situation in 2025.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></p><div>

</div><!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 121; Value: 1 --><div>
    </div><div style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->114<!-- Field: /Sequence --></p></div><div>
    </div><div style="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><p style="margin: 0pt">&#160;</p></div><div>
    </div><!-- Field: /Page --><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Provision for Income Taxes</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">We had provision for income
taxes of RMB6.4 million and RMB0.1 million (US$13 thousand) in 2024 and 2025, respectively.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Net Loss from Continuing Operations</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">As a result of the foregoing,
our net loss from continuing operations decreased by 48.5% to RMB36.6 million (US$5.2 million) in 2025 from RMB71.0 million in 2024.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Net Loss from Discontinued Operations</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Our net loss from discontinued
operations decreased by 70.7% to RMB2.7 million (US$0.4 million) in 2024 from RMB9.2 million in 2024.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b>Year Ended December 31, 2024 Compared to Year
Ended December 31, 2023</b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">On July 21, 2025, Xinjiang
Xinyouzhong Marketing Co., Ltd. (&#8220;Xinjiang Xinyouzhong&#8221;), an indirectly wholly-owned subsidiary of the Company, entered into
an equity transfer agreement (the &#8220;Agreement&#8221;) with Singularity Digital Marketing (Guangzhou) Co., Ltd. (&#8220;Singularity
Digital&#8221;), a related party controlled by Mr. Zhenfei Wu, our Chief Marketing Officer. Pursuant to the Agreement, Xinjiang Xinyouzhong
sold all of its 51% equity interest in Zhuhai Shengguang Zhongshuo Digital Marketing Co., Ltd. (&#8220;Shengguang Zhongshuo&#8221;) to
Singularity Digital. This disposal represented that we completely exited from all marketing and branding services operations. The disposal
of marketing and branding services business represented a strategic shift that had a major effect on our operations and financial results,
and was accounted for as discontinued operation. Accordingly, results of operations related to marketing and branding business have been
reflected in the accompanying consolidated financial statements as discontinued operation for all periods presented.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">We&#8217;ve restated the
consolidated balance sheet as of December 31, 2024 and consolidated statements of operation, comprehensive loss, changes in shareholder&#8217;s
equity and cash flows for the years ended December 31, 2023 and 2024, as we identified fraudulent acts conducted by certain employees
through fabricating the agency fees of the Group&#8217;s workspace membership business in specific workspace projects to earn kickback
from the real estate agencies. You should consider the information provided under Note 3 of our financial statements. The discussion
of year-over-year comparisons under this section for periods between 2025 and 2024, and 2024 and 2023 has reflected the impact of restatement.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">However, the Company&#8217;s
management believes that such retroactive adjustment of discontinue operation and restatement does not cause material change to the description
of the comparison of the Company&#8217;s operating results for the year ended December 31, 2024 to the year ended December 31, 2023 included
in its annual report on Form 20-F for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2024. For a detailed description of the comparison of our operating
results for the year ended December 31, 2023 to the year ended December 31, 2022, see &#8220;Item 5.A. Operating Results &#8212; Results
of Operations &#8212; Year Ended December 31, 2023 Compared to Year Ended December 31, 2022&#8221; of our annual report on Form 20-F
for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2023 filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission on April 25, 2024.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b>Non-GAAP Financial Measures</b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">To supplement our consolidated
financial statements, which are prepared and presented in accordance with U.S. GAAP, we use the following non-GAAP financial measures
for our consolidated results: EBITDA (including EBITDA margin), adjusted EBITDA (including adjusted EBITDA margin) and adjusted net loss
from continuing operations. We believe that EBITDA, adjusted EBITDA and adjusted net loss from continuing operations help understand
and evaluate our core operating performance.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"></p><div>

</div><!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 122; Value: 1 --><div>
    </div><div style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->115<!-- Field: /Sequence --></p></div><div>
    </div><div style="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><p style="margin: 0pt">&#160;</p></div><div>
    </div><!-- Field: /Page --><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">EBITDA, adjusted EBITDA and
adjusted net loss from continuing operations are presented to enhance investors&#8217; overall understanding of our financial performance
and should not be considered a substitute for, or superior to, the financial information prepared and presented in accordance with U.S.
GAAP. Investors are encouraged to review the reconciliation of the historical non-GAAP financial measures to their most directly comparable
GAAP financial measures. As EBITDA, adjusted EBITDA and adjusted net loss from continuing operations have material limitations as analytical
metrics and may not be calculated in the same manner by all companies, they may not be comparable to other similarly titled measures
used by other companies.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">In light of the foregoing
limitations, you should not consider EBITDA, adjusted EBITDA and adjusted net loss from continuing operations as substitutes for, or
superior to, net loss prepared in accordance with U.S. GAAP. We encourage investors and others to review our financial information in
its entirety and not rely on any single financial measure. For more information on these non-GAAP financial measures, please see the
table below.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">EBITDA represents net loss
before interest expense, net, provision for income taxes, depreciation of property and equipment and amortization of intangible assets.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Adjusted EBITDA represents
net loss before (1) interest expense/(income), net, other income, net, provision for income taxes, gain on disposal of long-term investments
and loss/(gain) on disposal of subsidiaries and (2) certain non-cash expenses, consisting of share-based compensation expense, impairment
loss on long-term investments, impairment loss on long-lived assets and long-term prepaid expenses, depreciation of property and equipment,
amortization of intangible assets, change in fair value of warrant liability and change in fair value of put option liability, which
we do not believe are reflective of our core operating performance during the periods presented.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Adjusted net loss from continuing
operations represents net loss before share-based compensation expense, impairment loss on long-lived assets and long-term prepaid expenses,
impairment loss on long-term investments, change in fair value of warrant liability, change in fair value of put option liability, gain
on disposal of long-term investments and loss/(gain) on disposal of subsidiaries.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">The following table sets
forth a reconciliation of net loss to EBITDA and adjusted EBITDA for the periods indicated:</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; border-spacing: 0px;">
